comments.text:
Very cool to see PyPI put more emphasis towards exposing provenance info. It would be even cooler if trusted publishing would finally support reusable workflows (
https://github.com/pypi/warehouse/issues/11096
).

If the tax law is inconsistent (as some of the comments seem to indicate), does that mean that we don't have to pay any tax or even are entitled to a large tax credit?  After all, Lean supports the principle of explosion (
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Principle_of_explosion
).
